+  "land": {
+    "_what": "The ground battle's own rows (the ground battle sound designer, 21 Nov 2026, release 2), for Brian's ask that the Normandy battle feel as intense as watching Saving Private Ryan: close cracks and snaps, every gun heard, louder and more intense when the camera is low and close. The film is a feel reference only: nothing is taken from it. Read by LandSound (the 3D game's ground battle); every number has a default in its code, so a mix without this block plays as v4 did. Only real recordings: a list left empty keeps its moment silent until a real take passes Brian's ear.",
+    "closeView": {
+      "_how": "Down among the men the whole battle is louder: every world sound (the battle beds, engines, shots, blasts, voices; not the place's wind, not the music) is lifted by dB read off this table by the camera's height over the ground (linear between rows, held at the ends). The master limiter (buses.master) keeps the stack under its ceiling.",
+      "dbByCameraHeight": [[0, 3.0], [4, 3.0], [20, 1.5], [80, 0.0]],
+      "_why": "Brian on the air battle, 21 Nov 16:20Z: 'when you behind the plane view make it louder and more intense'; asked again for the ground battle (louder and more intense when the camera is low and close). +3 dB, as the air's closeView (+3.1)."
+    },
+    "cracks": {
+      "_how": "A rifle or machine-gun round whose line passes within `within` metres of the ear cracks there, before the shot itself is heard from the muzzle (a bullet outruns its sound; its shock wave cracks where it passes). within and the shortest gap between two cracks are read off the tables by the camera's height over the ground; only shooters more than fromShooterMoreThan off. Level dbAt0 + dbPerMetre x the miss distance. A machine-gun burst passing near is a run: a stretch of one `run` recording (take, from, length of its firing part) as long as the burst plus runTail, no closer together than runGap. One a burst: the burst's other rounds are in the run.",
+      "withinByCameraHeight": [[0, 25], [4, 20], [20, 12], [80, 12]],
+      "gapByCameraHeight": [[0, 0.08], [4, 0.1], [20, 0.25]],
+      "fromShooterMoreThan": 25,
+      "single": ["bullet_crack"],
+      "run": [["bullets_incoming_01", 0.03, 1.53], ["bullets_incoming_02", 0.02, 2.14]],
+      "runTail": 0.25,
+      "runGap": 0.6,
+      "dbAt0": -2,
+      "dbPerMetre": -0.3,
+      "_why": "v4 cracked only within 12 m at most 4 times a second, wherever the camera was: on the Normandy run 146 cracks in 277 s. Down among the men (the eye is the ear under 4 m) the zone is 20 to 25 m and the gap 0.08 to 0.1 s: rounds passing within 25 m crack loud enough to make a man duck."
+    },
+    "groundStrikes": {
+      "_how": "A rifle or machine-gun round that missed and struck the ground within `within` metres of the ear, the camera lower than cameraBelow: the strike in the earth (one of `dirt`, heard as it lands) and, whineChance of the time but no closer together than whineGap, a ricochet whining off: a piece of `whines` (take, from, cut) or a whole `ricochet` take. One a burst.",
+      "within": 12,
+      "cameraBelow": 20,
+      "dirt": [],
