+      "_whines": "single ricochets cut at their own onsets (measured: each rises 10 dB or more within 10 ms) out of rakurka's Incoming Ricochets (approved as bullets_incoming_01/02): twelve whines from one approved recording, so the same one is rarely heard twice",
+      "ricochet": ["ricochet_01"],
+      "db": -4
+    },
+    "mgClose": {
+      "_how": "The land battle's close machine-gun takes by army (over byNation.mg). Every round fired is heard and no more: a burst plays from its take's first shot for its rounds / rate seconds (LandPlay.BurstOf: an MG 42 1,200 a minute in bursts of 7 to 10, the Americans' M1919 and BAR about 8 a second in 5 or 6), then `tail` seconds faded over tailFade (farTail for the far takes, whose echo rolls on longer). parts: each take's firing (seconds; measured where the take is within 20 dB of its loudest). A take whose firing is shorter than the burst gives way to one long enough; if none is, the whole take plays.",
